From: Ilia Alshanetsky <ilia@ilia.ws>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] Avoid copying the type AST at each LowCardinality level

CreateColumnFromAst() bound the LowCardinality child with
`const auto nested = GetASTChildElement(ast, 0)`, which copies the whole
subtree. Nested LowCardinality(Nullable(...)) levels each made another
copy while the recursion held the earlier ones, so peak memory grew with
depth times subtree width. Binding the child by reference removes the
copies.
---
 clickhouse/columns/factory.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/clickhouse/columns/factory.cpp b/clickhouse/columns/factory.cpp
--- a/clickhouse/columns/factory.cpp
+++ b/clickhouse/columns/factory.cpp
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
             break;
         }
         case TypeAst::LowCardinality: {
-            const auto nested = GetASTChildElement(ast, 0);
+            const auto& nested = GetASTChildElement(ast, 0);
             if (settings.low_cardinality_as_wrapped_column) {
                 switch (nested.code) {
                     // TODO (nemkov): update this to maximize code reuse.
